---
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---
<Base title="About">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      I'm a computer science student at the University of Michigan. I like building things that run on their own and can
      be checked: models that publish their picks before the game starts, and art that draws itself.
    </p>
    <p>
      As an analyst for Michigan Edge, the university's sports analytics club, I built three game predictors on my own: <a href="/projects/nfl-predictor/">Fourth and Why</a> for the NFL, <a href="/projects/mlb-predictor/">Full Count</a> for baseball and <a href="/projects/nba-predictor/">Tip-Off</a> for the NBA.
      Each is tested on games it never trained on and runs as a live app that keeps its own data current.
    </p>
    <p>
      I also make games. <a href="/projects/nightfall/">Nightfall</a> is a Godot horror game I built alone, about hunting a wendigo through a forest at night. With a small team, I've led programming and design on seven indie games, shipped as
      Windows releases.
    </p>
    <p><a href={SITE.cv}>Download my CV</a> (PDF) or email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
    <h2>Education</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>University of Michigan</strong>, Ann Arbor: BSE in Computer Science, expected May 2028.<br />
      <strong>Michigan State University</strong>: BSE in Computer Science, 2025–2026.
    </p>
    <h2 id="credits">Credits</h2>
    <p>
      The home page rebuilds God's group from Michelangelo's <cite>The Creation of Adam</cite> (Sistine Chapel ceiling, c. 1511),
      using the public-domain photograph <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Michelangelo_-_Creation_of_Adam_(cropped).jpg">Michelangelo - Creation of Adam (cropped)<Arrow /></a> from Wikimedia Commons.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Nightfall renders use the game's own free-to-use models and sounds, with CC0 textures from Poly Haven and ambientCG.
    </p>
    <p>Typefaces: Gloock, Newsreader and IBM Plex Mono, under the SIL Open Font License.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
